From 2df2bec6597fd13eea00c011953aaa463d86734b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:00:15 +0200
Subject: [EME] Add Widevine to the external CDM backend

https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328385

Reviewed by NOBODY (OOPS!).

Add com.widevine.alpha to the GStreamer external CDM backend, driving
the Chromium Widevine CDM in process through inputstream.adaptive's
cdm_adapter, vendored and built in a unit of its own because it needs
exceptions and RTTI. KeyHandleValueVariant gains a
BoxPtr<ExternalCdmSession> alternative under ENABLE(EXTERNAL_CDM),
mirroring the Thunder BoxPtr<OpenCDMSession>, so a decryptor reaches the
CDM by key id while the key bytes stay inside it. CDMInstanceExternalCDM
owns one CdmAdapter per instance and routes its host callbacks onto the
main thread; the session maps requestLicense, updateLicense and
close/remove onto CreateSessionAndGenerateRequest, UpdateSession and
Close/RemoveSession, and fills the key store from OnSessionKeysChange.
CDMProxyExternalCDM dispatches on the key-handle variant: ClearKey keeps
the libgcrypt path, Widevine builds a cdm::InputBuffer_2 and decrypts in
place at L3, carrying the cbcs crypt/skip pattern, the subsample map
from the protection metadata and the buffer presentation timestamp in
microseconds.

This Widevine CDM returns kNoKey from Decrypt() for video and yields
pictures only through DecryptAndDecodeFrame(), so encrypted video is
handled by webkitexternalcdmvideodec, a GstVideoDecoder that hands
encrypted AV1, VP9, VP8 and H.264 with the Widevine protection system to
the CDM to decrypt and decode into I420 and its 10- and 12-bit variants,
clear-lead frames included. H.264 is passed as Annex B with the
parameter sets ahead of each keyframe, the form the CDM expects. Ranked
above the decryptor, parsebin routes encrypted Widevine video to this
decoder while audio and ClearKey keep the decryptor, and the sample
handling common to both is factored out. The decoder serialises its own
CDM calls and the instance publishes its adapter so clear frames decode
before the first key arrives. The factory offers Widevine when the CDM
blob is present.

ClearKey is unchanged and the feature stays behind ENABLE_EXTERNAL_CDM.

